	(text "VALVE-COMMON RELAY (hardware design section 7).\nK1 G5NB-1A-E, 5 V 125R coil fed from V_BUCK, feeds AC_L to the COM terminals. With K1 open no valve\nhas power, whatever a shorted triac, TVS or opto-triac does. It closes only when Q1 AND Q2 conduct.\nQ1: on while expander bit RLY_ON is high. DRV_EN low resets the expander and R12 turns Q1 off in 0.1 ms.\nQ2: on while the relay detector sees edges on KA. R89, C51, D22 pump the reservoir C50; R14 and R90\n    (two, so that one open resistor only doubles the time) drain it. Gate about 2.7 V while toggling.\n    Q2 lets go 0.10 to 1.45 s after the last edge, within 2.19 s if the pin stops high\n    (simulated corners of review A2; the long end is a low-threshold Q2 when hot).\nR93, R94, R95: read-back of the node between Q1 and Q2 on GPIO7. 3.05 V = Q2 off, 0 V = Q2 on.\nD23 SMBJ48CA clamps COM while K1 is open and takes the inductive kick when it opens under load.\nJP1: open. Bridge only if the relay is not fitted (then the fault analysis of section 8.5 is void).\nLAYOUT: no test pad on RLY_G2, KB_N1 or KB_N0. Surround the gate node of Q2 with ground: a leakage\npath from any rail to that node is the only way to hold Q2 on. Keep this pump (R89, C51, D22) at\nleast 10 mm from the gate-drive pump (R29, C22, D7), and turn C51 at right angles to C22.\nK1 is through-hole, inserted from the bottom side."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.12 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5cce5ac4-108d-57c0-abbc-f7e61579ab33")
	)
	(text "R28: 8-zone build only.\nNot fitted: bit P14 reads high,\nfirmware runs four zones."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 121.92 248.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8291052a-f4a3-5433-86ee-f40bf6d55da6")
	)
	(text "Valve-common relay: coil current passes Q1 and Q2 in series"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.85 46.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8e8c1ba7-64fd-5d26-95a7-c109956ad812")
	)
	(text "16-bit I2C expander, address 0x74, held in reset by DRV_EN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 46.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ad805631-a3fc-5ff5-9854-ab1fed69f4b2")
	)
	(text "EXPANDER (section 8.2). U5 TCA9539: every pin is an input while RESET is low, which is whenever no\nvalve runs. A valve is on when its bit is an output and low: P00 to P03 Z1 to Z4, P04 MV, P10 to P13\nZ5 to Z8. P05 RLY_ON is on when high. P14 reads the build variant, P15 the sensor supply fault.\nRN1, RN2, R96 hold the valve pins at V_DRV, not 3V3, so an off opto LED never sees reverse voltage.\nRN3 holds the four spare pins low. RN2 is fitted on both builds."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 269.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c35a4dd3-f19c-5cf7-a806-1b9dc0e3e132")
	)
	(text "Defined levels on every expander pin while it is in reset"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 163.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f0342be6-35ac-569f-84aa-edce9f1a9153")
	)
